{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:cf94f5ed09fd5ba0","name":"Officer (CL 8)","source":{"id":"source:reference-cf94f5ed09fd5ba0","title":"Officer (CL 8)","revision":23072,"timestamp":"2024-09-15T13:32:37Z","sha256":"98feca3066cdb1ab512344998477447c78116ac3d4e1ae64e17f92549e14abe9","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=23072","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Officer%20%28CL%208%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-cf94f5ed09fd5ba0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Officer described here represents a leader who goes out in the field, commanding alongside her troops. She is trained in quickly assessing the battlefield and deploying her troops in the most effective way possible- with the hope of keeping losses in both soldiers and equipment to a minimum. This sort of Officer leads by example, giving orders from the front lines of combat, often scoffing at the plans concocted by the higher-ups in the safety of the rear deployment zone. An Officer must make tough decisions, putting her troops in extremely hazardous, and sometimes suicidal, positions to get the job done. Officers carry little in the way of weapons or armor, relying on other troops for protection and transportation. Depending on their actual rank, this \"entourage\" can be anything from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bodyguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bodyguard","referenceId":"reference:998e41b432f4d199"}," and an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"}," all the way up to a brigade of troops, heavily armored tanks, and a contingent of Battle Droids. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["It is important to remember that an Officer's rank isn't necessarily tied to their level as a game character- a Brigade Commander might have fewer Heroic Levels than the Lieutenant of a platoon, especially if that Lieutenant has seen intense combat. Heroic Levels represent a character's participation in action-filled adventures or missions of deep intrigue, not the number of years they spent as a desk jockey. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["The Chain of Command"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["An advantage to including an Officer- as well as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commander"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commander","referenceId":"reference:16af7be312e1840b"}," or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commando Squad Leader"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commando_Squad_Leader","referenceId":"reference:b89fdf754af0b7c7"}," in an encounter is that such a character effectively increases the challenge provided by each individual ally he brings with him. When designing encounters using officers, the Gamemasters should keep in mind that the other enemies in the encounter will be slightly more powerful (though not enough to adjust their CL); although this might not make any difference in an encounter that features only a small number of enemies, the effect becomes cumulative when more enemies are added to the encounter.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Each additional enemy is one that is more likely to successfully use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Aid Another"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Aid_Another","referenceId":"reference:276932074aab1852"}," Action for its allies, causing the heroes' ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defense"}," scores to drop while enemy attack bonuses rise. Add to that the Officer's ability to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Share Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Share_Talents"}," (effectively giving ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," opponents access to abilities usually reserved for heroic characters), and an encounter's difficulty can jump drastically. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," enemies under an Officer's command can become tougher to hit and can deal more damage, so Gamemasters who include large numbers of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," enemies in an encounter with an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," should be careful to monitor the effects of an Officer's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," on the overall encounter difficulty.\n"]},"\n","\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Officer Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Officers are almost never encountered alone-even on \"solitary' missions. They are often accompanied by a retinue of noncommissioned officers and enlisted personnel. The Officer presented here works best as the commander of a squad of 6-10 soldiers or a platoon of 20-30 soldiers, with accompanying support ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," (the exact number depends on the CL of the encounter). This sort of Officer is a capable fighter in her own right but works best when she is able to direct the movement of her troops.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An Officer might be assigned to lead a group of highly trained specialists in order to complete a specific mission. Typical allies include ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commandos"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commandos"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Elite Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Elite_Soldiers"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Medics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Medics_(CL_3)"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilots"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilots_(CL_5)"},"- possibly with the Officer being the least powerful member of the group.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Officer Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +13\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Bocce, 4 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 21 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 19), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 20, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wi